+### G58 — custom-stencil tagging: reserved base 200, capture-the-state, refcounted r.CustomDepth; the SHOW/match is what fails late (stencil-capture S2)
+Tag the anomaly target's renderable mesh primitives with a reserved Custom Stencil value so the GPU rasterises the silhouette
+(`SetRenderCustomDepth(true)` + `SetCustomDepthStencilValue(tag)`); `r.CustomDepth 3` (EnabledWithStencil) at runtime, no host
+config. Load-bearing details: **(1)** capture-the-state-you-mutate — save each component's prior `{bRenderCustomDepth,
+CustomDepthStencilValue}` and restore EXACTLY (never assume 0; the host may already use custom stencil for outlines). **(2)**
+reserved base = **200**, tag = `200 + fire index` — clear of the small values host/UE selection systems use, headroom under 256
+(per-fire ids => free multi-actor). **(3)** `r.CustomDepth` enable/disable is **refcounted** so the capture run, the debug viz,
+and manual tagging can each hold it without one disabling it under another. **(4)** the gate-viz material (`M_AnomalyStencilViz`,
+authored by `tools/create_stencil_viz_material.py`) is a Post Process material — the Python tool tripped on GUESSED 5.1 enum
+names (correct: `BlendableLocation.BL_AFTER_TONEMAPPING`, `SceneTextureId.PPI_CUSTOM_STENCIL` / `PPI_POST_PROCESS_INPUT0`) and on
+a Lerp width mismatch (`PostProcessInput0.Color` is float4 — mask it to RGB to match the float3 green; Emissive is float3); the
+If node's `"A > B"` pins are fragile, prefer plain math nodes (Subtract/Abs/Clamp/OneMinus/Lerp). VERIFY material enum/pin names
+against engine source, and note Python `MaterialEditingLibrary` does NOT expose the shader compile-error list (type-check the
+graph by construction). **(5)** hide-type detection for Stage 3: `missing_object` hides via `SetActorHiddenInGame(true)` ->
+`IsVisible()==false`, so "is the target currently rendering" is a clean runtime signal for projected-vs-stencil box source.
+(2026-06-30.)
