+### G59 — AInstancedFoliageActor is a bad injection/capture target: level-spanning bounds AND its HISM ignores actor-hide (stencil-capture S3a)
+Two independent reasons the level's `AInstancedFoliageActor` must be **excluded** from the renderable-visible target pool
+(pulled forward from Stage 3b): **(1)** its actor bounds are the **union of ALL foliage instances** → span the whole level → the
+m7 projected box is grotesque (min far off-screen, e.g. `bbox_norm ≈ [-5.1, -3.1, …]`). **(2)** `missing_object`/`flicker` hide via
+`SetActorHiddenInGame(true)` and the actor reports `IsHidden()==true` (so the box-source detector picks the projected "hole" box),
+BUT the foliage **HISM keeps rendering** — actor-hidden does NOT propagate to the foliage system's own visibility path — so the
+Custom-Stencil silhouette persists on a frame we labelled hide-type. The actor-hide / still-drawing **mismatch is foliage-specific**:
+a standalone `UInstancedStaticMeshComponent`/`UHierarchicalInstancedStaticMeshComponent` on a normal actor DOES respect
+`SetActorHiddenInGame` (standard `UPrimitiveComponent::ShouldRender` owner-hidden path) and has sane per-component bounds — so the
+exclusion is scoped to the **foliage container only**, NOT all ISM/HISM (a populated ISM crate stays a legit target). Implemented in
+the shared per-actor classifier `AnomalyViewport::ClassifyRenderableVisibleLive` (the single source of truth — selector + auto +
+dashboard all inherit, per G51), matched by **reflected class NAME** `"InstancedFoliageActor"` walking the class chain — a typed
+`IsA<AInstancedFoliageActor>()` would pull in a **Foliage-module dependency** (`/Script/Foliage`), which the name match avoids
+(keeps the core dep set + game-agnostic label-free convention intact). BANKED: if a future requirement wants foliage AS a target,
+the hide-detection needs per-instance handling (out of scope for v1). (2026-07-01.)
